== Biography ==
'''Spencer Lafayette Glasgow''' was born on 12 September 1855 in Newberry County, South Carolina. The family reconstruction names [[Glasgow-2440|Archibald C. Glasgow]] and [[Griffith-14004|Caroline Griffith]] as his parents. A family account identifies his wife as Sara Jane Todd, gives their marriage as 17 December 1876, and names eight children: Obie Irene, Thomas Jefferson, Effie Joree, Braxton, Ada Lutitia, William Ross, Wade Lafayette, and Kemper Talmage.<ref name="FamilyAccount">[https://yanceyfamilygenealogy.org/LifesWeaving/GlasgowToddDempsey.html ''Life's Weaving'', “Spencer LaFayette Glasgow and Sara Jane Todd Descendants”], family reconstruction; accessed 27 September 2026. The account names Archibald and Caroline, supplies Spencer's birth date and describes the wife, children, death and burial.</ref>

Spencer was buried at Mountain Home Cemetery in Franklin County, Alabama. The Find a Grave memorial gives his death as 6 February 1936 in Belgreen; the family account gives 5 February 1936. The original Alabama death certificate has not been inspected, so the one-day difference remains open.<ref name="Grave">[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/40595776/spencer_lafayette-glasgow Find a Grave memorial 40595776], Spencer Lafayette Glasgow (12 September 1855 – 6 February 1936), Mountain Home Cemetery, Franklin County, Alabama; accessed 27 September 2026.</ref><ref name="FamilyAccount" />

== Research Notes ==
The former duplicate profile used the middle name ''Leonidus'' and gave a death on 5 September 1936 at Spruce Pine. Both profiles agreed on Spencer's exact 12 September 1855 birth at Newberry and attached the same father. The family account and cemetery memorial identify Spencer ''Lafayette'' with this birth date and parents, so the two profiles were merged on 27 September 2026. ''Leonidus'' and the September death remain documented as former tree assertions; no independent record has been found to support them. The Alabama death certificate should resolve the February day and place.

Spencer was formerly attached to [[Glasgow-2439|James Glasgow]] and [[Glasgow-3042|Sarah Glasgow]]; James died in 1831 and Sarah in 1847, before Spencer's birth. The current Archibald and Caroline parent links follow the family reconstruction and remain uncertain pending a direct record.

